overview:
  eyebrow: The idea
  heading: Bring families back to the work site
  lead: Some corporations invest in a daycare on site, so parents can visit their kids during the day. Family Cooperative Work Sites asks how that idea can reach everyone, with safety and proximity both achieved.
  sectionTitle: Work and home used to share a roof
  paragraphs:
    - For most of human history, work and family lived side by side. Farms, workshops and shops were run by households, and children grew up alongside the work. The factory, the office and the commute pulled the two apart.
    - Imagine someone doing blue-collar work taking a break to spend it with their own children. This initiative flows out of <a href="/rethink-human/" class="font-semibold text-blazing-flame-500 underline">ReTHINK Human</a>, the branch of Training Adam that starts over on what a human is.
